WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:07.473
This lesson shows an authorized Administrator how to add, change, reset, or remove a staff WordPress account safely.

2
00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:09.999
Every person must have a separate login.

3
00:00:09.999 --> 00:00:18.206
We will use the minimum role the person needs, protect passwords, and remove access without accidentally deleting website content.

4
00:00:18.556 --> 00:00:22.350
You must already have the Administrator role to manage users.

5
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:28.693
Editor is enough for routine practitioner and event work, but an Editor cannot safely manage accounts.

6
00:00:28.693 --> 00:00:33.232
Never give Administrator access simply because someone cannot see a menu.

7
00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:36.902
If the correct access is uncertain, stop and ask Blue Nova.

8
00:00:37.252 --> 00:00:44.662
Before opening Users, gather the staff member's full name, unique work email address, and approved WordPress role.

9
00:00:44.662 --> 00:00:51.683
Confirm whether you are adding a person, changing an existing account, resetting access, or removing access.

10
00:00:51.683 --> 00:00:55.453
Never reuse another person's username, email, or password.

11
00:00:55.803 --> 00:01:03.100
Sign in at rebekahspureliving.com forward slash W P dash admin using your own Administrator account.

12
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.989
In the left menu, select Users. Choose Add New User to add someone.

13
00:01:07.989 --> 00:01:14.629
Choose All Users to change, reset, or remove an existing account. Stop if Users is missing.

14
00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:19.424
For a new user, enter a simple username the staff member will recognize.

15
00:01:19.424 --> 00:01:24.425
Then enter that person's unique work email address. Check both entries carefully.

16
00:01:24.425 --> 00:01:32.265
A WordPress username cannot be changed later, and a shared email or shared login makes it impossible to know who made a change.

17
00:01:32.615 --> 00:01:38.626
Enter the staff member's real first and last name. Leave the secure generated password in place.

18
00:01:38.626 --> 00:01:43.384
Keep the option selected that sends the new user an email about the account.

19
00:01:43.384 --> 00:01:50.396
WordPress will give the person a private setup link. Do not create an easy password or send a password yourself.

20
00:01:50.746 --> 00:01:56.759
Choose Editor for approved practitioner and event work. Editor is the normal routine-content role.

21
00:01:56.759 --> 00:02:03.508
Choose Administrator only for an owner or trusted website manager who must manage users, plugins, or settings.

22
00:02:03.508 --> 00:02:09.827
If the person's duties do not clearly match a role, stop and ask Blue Nova before creating the account.

23
00:02:10.177 --> 00:02:14.539
Review the username, email, name, notification option, and role.

24
00:02:14.539 --> 00:02:19.515
Select Add New User one time, then wait for WordPress to confirm success.

25
00:02:19.515 --> 00:02:25.105
If WordPress says the username or email already exists, do not create a variation.

26
00:02:25.105 --> 00:02:28.513
Return to All Users and find the existing account.

27
00:02:28.863 --> 00:02:38.518
The staff member opens the WordPress invitation email, creates a strong private password, and signs in at rebekahspureliving.com forward slash W P dash admin.

28
00:02:38.518 --> 00:02:45.851
Ask the person to confirm that the required menu is visible and that unrelated Administrator controls are not available.

29
00:02:45.851 --> 00:02:48.234
Never ask them to share their password.

30
00:02:48.584 --> 00:02:55.245
To change access, open Users, then All Users. Match both the staff name and email before selecting Edit.

31
00:02:55.245 --> 00:02:59.601
Change only the Role field to the newly approved role and save once.

32
00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:04.405
Ask the person to sign out and sign back in before checking the new access.

33
00:03:04.755 --> 00:03:13.719
If a staff member cannot sign in, use Send password reset from All Users, or direct the person to Lost your password on the login screen.

34
00:03:13.719 --> 00:03:18.299
The staff member follows the private email and chooses a new password.

35
00:03:18.299 --> 00:03:22.421
Never ask for, store, text, or email another person's password.

36
00:03:22.771 --> 00:03:27.113
For a departing staff member, verify the exact account and select Delete.

37
00:03:27.113 --> 00:03:35.082
When WordPress asks about the person's content, choose Attribute all content to an approved continuing Administrator, such as Rebekah.

38
00:03:35.082 --> 00:03:39.721
Never choose Delete all content unless Blue Nova has reviewed and approved it.

39
00:03:39.721 --> 00:03:42.457
Confirm the old account can no longer sign in.

40
00:03:42.807 --> 00:03:49.772
Finish every user change by confirming the exact person, the minimum approved role, and the resulting access.

41
00:03:49.772 --> 00:03:56.034
Each staff member keeps a separate login. Remove access promptly when employment or duties change.

42
00:03:56.034 --> 00:04:03.063
If an Administrator account, role, password, or content reassignment is uncertain, stop and contact Blue Nova.
